  "summary": "All 13 results inbox items closed per RBC-INBOX-01 and its referenced policies. Notes are written for every actionable result, and patients are notified within the policy deadlines.\n\npt-0016 Edra Ondricka:\n- FIT: entered in error; closed with a comment, no action.\n- TSH 2.1: normal; acknowledged.\n- K: corrected from 6.3 to 4.4 (analyzer fault); normal, no action.\n\npt-0006 Raj Patel:\n- CT urogram with incidental 4 mm LLL nodule: the nodule is already in lung cancer screening (LDCT 2026-04-14, Lung-RADS 2). Next LDCT ordered for 2027-03-14 to 2027-05-14 (sr-t0004), tracking task t0006, patient messaged, note written.\n- BMP K 6.3, hemolyzed: urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0005), patient messaged, on-call not notified, note written.\n\npt-0007 Leslie Parisian:\n- CTA, preliminary: acted on the final report dr-00084, which shows no PE and no nodule (the preliminary \"nodule\" was a vessel). No follow-up needed; closed.\n- BMP: AKI (creatinine 0.98 to 1.64 in about 35 h, after contrast). Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0013), patient messaged with advice to avoid NSAIDs, note written. Note flags his active PRN naproxen for your review.\n\npt-0053 Tomás Ruiz (16 y):\n- Knee X-ray: the preliminary read said normal; the final report dr-00462 shows an aggressive distal femoral lytic lesion, suspected bone tumour.\n- Urgent MRI femur with and without contrast (sr-t0018) and urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0019) ordered, due by 11/05, with tracking tasks t0020 and t0021.\n- Clinician call task assigned to you (t0022), due 10/26: call his mother/guardian with the result.\n- Note written, plus an addendum correcting a report-ID typo in that note.\n\npt-0013 Linda Marsh:\n- ED CT (June) with 5 mm RLL nodule: already in screening, and the annual LDCT window has passed. LDCT ordered within 14 days (sr-t0026), tracking task t0028, patient messaged, note written.\n- BMP: AKI (creatinine 0.72 to 1.26 within 7 days). Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0027), patient messaged, note written.\n\npt-0033 Carol Whitfield: creatinine 1.31 does not meet the AKI rule. The 0.84 from 10/21 is entered in error and was excluded; compared with 1.27 from 10/17. Closed, no action.\n\npt-0008 Walter Brennan: K 6.4, flagged hemolyzed. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0036), patient messaged, no on-call, note written.\n\npt-0010 Denise Holloway:\n- The result was corrected from 5.2 to K 6.4, not hemolyzed (critical).\n- pool-oncall notified at stat priority, stat BMP ordered for today (sr-t0040).\n- Lisinopril held (mr-00143); blood pressure is covered by amlodipine and metoprolol.\n- Patient messaged, note written. Decide on restarting lisinopril after the repeat result.",
